          %title Contents
          %hr/
          %p
            %strong Update Dec 2022.
            At long last, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHCb+collaboration"} LHCb collaboration
            in Dec 2022 announced (
            %a{:href => "#LHCB22"}> LHCB22
            ) that they had all along been mis-attributing hadronic backgrounds in the measurement of kaonic decays of B-mesons to electron pairs (as some people had
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "http://resonaances.blogspot.com/2021/03/thoughts-on-rk.html?showComment=1617397775790&m=1#c6699295970247538741"} suspected
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{K^{\ast}}
            disappear, and with it most of the other apparent anomalies, too (
            %a{:href => "#CFFPSV22"}> CFFPSV22
            ). For more see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FixingTheBackgrounds"} below
          %p This seems to mean that all the discussion on this page here is essentially obsolete as far as its particle physics content goes – what remains is maybe just of historical/sociological interest.
