                have moved towards the Standard Model, but this actually improves the New Physics fits.
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              The set of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s \ell \ell
              anomalies are alive and a global coherence remains after the measurements in 2019 and 2020. While some key measurements have central values that have moved towards the Standard Model predictions, the overall consistency of the data and the global tension with respect to the Standard Model has not diminished (in fact this may even enhance the significance for New Physics). The New Physics fit is a good fit (with
              = succeed "-values" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significances"} statistical significances
            of pull away from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
            New Physics models:
          %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/AlgueroBsll19Fits.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
            %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
              from
              %a{:href => "#Alguero19"} Alguero 19
          %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/Koppenburg20PullSummary.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
            %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
              from
              %a{:href => "#Koppenburg20"} Koppenburg 20
          %h3#UpdatesIn2021 Updates in 2021
          %p#SignificanceMarch2021
            New measurements reported by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
            %a{:href => "https://home.cern/news/news/physics/intriguing-new-result-lhcb-experiment-cern"} in March 2021
            for the first time see deviation in a single decay channel at a statistical significance above
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3.1
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3.1 \sigma
          %p Implications for the significance across channels:
          %p
            %a{:href => "#HLN21"}> HLN 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              Naive combination of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_K
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{K*}
              measurements shows a deviation from the standard model above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 4
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4 \sigma
          %p
            %a{:href => "#GengEtAl21"}> Geng et al. 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              Motivated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
              LHCb’s new measurements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
              we quantify the combined level of discrepancy with the Standard Model and fit values of short-distance Wilson coefficients. A combination of the clean observables
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_K
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi K
                            %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{K^\ast}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo →
                    %mi μ
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_s \to \mu \mu
              alone results in a discrepancy with the Standard Model at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4.0
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4.0 \sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3.5
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3.5 \sigma
              in 2017. One-parameter scenarios with purely left-handed or with purely axial coupling to muons fit the data well and result in a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∼
                    %mn 5
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim 5 \sigma
              pull from the Standard Model.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#AltmannshoferStangl21"}> AlSt 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              With the recent updates
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              the case for new physics inrare B decays has been further strengthened.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              Even if only the theoretically clean LFU observables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              are considered, muon specific
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              Wilson coefficients for New Physics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              improve over the Standard Model by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
