                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{\Delta^2} \simeq 4.7 \sigma
          %p
            %a{:href => "#CFFIN21"}> CFFIN 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              With the recent result
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHCb"} LHCb
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3 \sigma
              level. Equally striking is the overall coherence of the picture that emerges, especially in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s \ell^+ \ell^-
              −transitions. As we shall show in this paper, combining all the
              = succeed "\u2212observables" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s \ell^+ \ell^-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significance"} significance
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4.6
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4.6 \sigma
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\ldots]
              A more structural way of addressing the flavor structure of the model is the idea of implementing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} Pati-Salam unification
          %p
            %a{:href => "#LIOS21"}> LIOS 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p we obtain the global significance to be 3.9 standard deviations
          %p
            %a{:href => "#MarzoccaTrifinopoulos21"}> MT 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              the combined significance of the deviation reaches
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4.7
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4.7\sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\ldots]
              the overall significance of the deviations in this channel is raised to even above
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 6
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 6\sigma
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Davighi21"}> Davighi 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              A highly conservative method for combining the various
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s \ell \ell
              anomalies, including the look-elsewhere effect, estimates their global significance to be 3.9σ. The combined set of discrepancies are by and large self-consistent with a common new physics origin involving muons.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Chang21"}> Chang 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              From the global fits to various
              = succeed "\u2212data," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mi l
                        %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi l
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to  s l^+ l^-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 5
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 5\sigma
              from the SM predictions. The new result (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.11769"}> 59
              ) further strengthens the lepton flavor universality violation. This anomaly alone convincingly indicates New Physics
          %p
            %a{:href => "#CFFIN21"}> CFFIN 21
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              striking is the overall coherence of the picture that emerges, especially in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s \ell^+ \ell^-
              −transitions. As we shall show in this paper, combining all the
              = succeed "\u2212observables" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s \ell^+ \ell^-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significance"} significance
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4.6
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4.6 \sigma
          %h3#UpdatesIn2022 Updates in 2022
          %p
            %a{:href => "#AliseEtAl2222"}> Alise et al. 22
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              We critically analyze the body of results that hints to the existence of New Physics from possible violations of lepton universality observed by the LHCb experiment.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
              the deviations from the Standard Model are at the 4.7σ level when including only the hadronic insensitive observables while it increases to 6.1σ when including also the hadronic sensitive ones.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              Scalar
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leptoquarks"} leptoquarks
          %p
            %a{:href => "#ACMM22"}> ACMM 22
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              when combining all tests of LFUV (like
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi K
                          %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{K^+}
              ) with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              decays involving muon pairs &amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack;, one finds a preference for new physics (NP) hypotheses of more than 7σ compared to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} SM
          %p
            %a{:href => "#PBD22"}> PBD22
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              We have used our improved scalar, vector and tensor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/form+factors"} form factors
              calculated in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_f = 2+1+1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
              \&amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack; Our improved form factors significantly sharpen the tension, which becomes particularly strong in the region below the charmonium resonances. For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1.1
                    %mo &lt;
