                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 6
                    %msup
                      %mi GeV
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1.1 \lt  q^2 \lt 6 GeV^2
              we find a tension of 4.7σ for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^+ \to K^+ \mu^+ \mu^-
              and 3.6σ for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^0 \to K^+ \mu^+ \mu^-
              with LHCb ’14A and 3.3σ for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^+ \to K^+ e^+ e^-
              with LHCb ’21
          %p
            %a{:href => "#PBD22b"}> PBD22b
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              We present the first fully relativistic determination of the scalar, vector and tensor form factors for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to K
              decays. &amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack; Using these form factors, we can calculate the SM branching fraction for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi μ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to K e(\mu)+ e(\mu)^-
              \&amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack; We find tensions above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3\sigma
              in the ratio of our result with LHCb, and above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 5
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 5\sigma
              in one instance for the low
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi q
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q^2
              bin.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Mahmoudi22"}> Mahmoudi 2022
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              The updated NP fits to rare B decays &amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack; follow the same trend as with the previous set of results favouring in particular new physics contributions in the Wilson coefficient
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mn 9
                        %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\mu_9
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_K
              can establish NP with 5σ significance already with less than 20
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi fb
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fb^{-1}
              of data. The main source of theory uncertainty in global fits is due to non-local hadronic contributions. However, different fits with different setups, inputs and statistical frameworks show a remarkable agreement so that the experimental observation of the discrepancy in these observables would be a clear sign of physics beyond the SM.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#IKW22"}> IKW22
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              Incorporating several recent developments of determinations of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to D^{(\ast)}
              form factors in the Standard Model (SM), we observe a 4.1σ deviation from the SM predictions.
            %p present data deviates from the SM predictions at 4.3σ.
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Soni22"}> Soni 2022
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p For almost a decade now, there have been persistent indications from all three major B-facilities of lepton universality violations (LUV) [1], [2–10], with a combined significance of 4.5σ [11]. In tree-level charge current decays, B → D(∗)τ(l)ν, the reactions involving τ seem to differ more from those involving muon or electron than predicted by the SM. Another class of reaction that is presenting an even stronger indications of lepton flavor universality violations is flavor changing neutral current decays which, in the SM are loop-level. At the quark-lepton level this is b → sl+l − for l = µ or e. The corresponding ratios of such reactions, RK(∗) etc which in the SM are supposed to be unity within O(few %), experimentally at LHCb [9] are found to be significantly different from unity i.e. O(≈ 30%) at around 3 or even possibly ≈ 4σ. Moreover, another rather strong indication of new physics (NP) that has been strengthened this year is the muon (g-2) anomaly. For well over a decade this was already around 3.5σ being the difference between the experimental measurements at BNL from about 2002 [12] to around 2006 [13] and the theory predictions based on dispersion relations, data driven approach [14].
            %p
              Recent confirmation by the Fermilab
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g-2)
              Collaboration [15] of the old BNL result has now increased the deviation from the data-driven theory prediction from the SM to about 4.2σ. The main point to bear in mind is that there are three anomalies, RD(∗) , RK(∗) and muon (g-2), and each of these is over three σ.
            %p So, the chances of at least one of these surviving the test of time and leading us to new physics is rather high,
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#FixingTheBackgrounds Fixing the backgrounds
          %p
            However,
            %a{:href => "#LHCB22"} LHCB22
            claims that re-analysis of hadronic backgrounds in kaonic decays makes the decay rate in the electron channel go down, so that the ratio
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{K^\ast}
            over the corresponding muon channel is accurately described by the standard model (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://twitter.com/axelmaas/status/1605159026441986049"} A. Maas, 20 Dec 2022
          %p This seems to make all the apparent anomalies disappear.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#CFFPSV22"}> CFFPSV22
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p we show that current data no longer provide strong hints for NP.
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#RelationToOtherAnomalies Relation to other anomalies
          %p
            There is possibly a relation between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            to anomalies currently observed in other processes, notably to the
            %a{:href => "anomalous+magnetic+moment#Anomalies"} anomalies
            observed in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+magnetic+moment"} anomalous magnetic moment
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            and/or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/muon"} muon
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ChiangOkada17"} Chiang-Okada 17
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+sector"} flavour sector
            (e.g.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#CrivellinHoferichter20"} Crivellin-Hoferichter 20
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/CrivellinRandAHints.jpg", :width => "300px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                graphics from
                %a{:href => "#CrivellinHoferichter20"} Crivellin-Hoferichter 20
          %blockquote
            %p
              (here “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              ” refers to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
              in various channels, “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              ” refers to anomalies in the the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+magnetic+moments"} anomalous magnetic moments
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/muon"} muon
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significances"} statistical significances
              of the effects seen)
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 10px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/CrivellinHintsForNewPhysics21.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#Crivellin21"} Crivellin 21, slide 15
          %p
            Indeed,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leptoquark"} leptoquark
            models preferred by the flavour anomalies (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Leptoquarks"} below
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significance"} statistical significance
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+magnetic+moment"} anomalous magnetic moment
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/muon"} muon
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "anomalous+magnetic+moment#Anomalies"} there
          %p
            Some authors therefore begin to speak jointly of
            %em muon anomalies
            (
            %a{:href => "#GST21"}> GST 21
            ).
          %p#KoppenburgListOfAnomalies
            Here is a list of experiments, all somehow related to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/muons"} muons
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 10px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/KoppenburgFlavourAnomaliesApril2021.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#KoppenburgScholarpedia"} Koppenburg Scholarp.
          %p
            (This is as of April 2021, see
            %a{:href => "http://www.scholarpedia.org/article/Rare_decays_of_b_hadrons#Prospects"} here
            for the source text with more details; also
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Koppenburg21"} Koppenburg 21, slide 44
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#KoppenburgAnomalies"} Koppenburg Fl. Anom.
          %p
            %br/
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 10px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/KoppenburgFlavourAnomaliesPattern.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#Koppenburg21"} Koppenburg 21, slide 53
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-model" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leptoquark"} leptoquark
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28g-2%29-anomaly"} (g-2)-anomaly
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cabibbo+anomaly"} Cabibbo anomaly
            at once:
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MarzoccaTrifinopoulos21"} Marzocca-Trifinopoulos 21
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#ACMM22"} ACMM22
            it is argued (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.08170.pdf#page=2"} footnote 3
            %a{:href => "W-boson#CDF22"} CDF collaboration 2022
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-boson"} W-boson
            is compatible with (in fact predicted by) the
            = succeed "-meson" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#Outlook Status and Outlook
          %p
            In conclusion, with currently available data, the observed flavour anomalies are possible signs of New Physics beyond the current
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/DordeiConclusion.jpg", :width => "740px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                graphics taken from
                %a{:href => "#Dordei18"} Dordei 18, slide 22
          %p
            %br/
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 10px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/TuningFLavourAnomaliesInterlocking.jpg", :width => "560px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#Tuning20"} Tuning 20
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            In any case, further and more sensitive experiments are needed to confirm and explore the effect, such as possibly the “
            %a{:href => "http://hilumilhc.web.cern.ch"}> HL-LHC
            ” or “HE-LHC” experiment. General outlook, prospects and suggestions for future collider design in this respect are discussed in detail in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AllanachGripaiosYou17"} Allanach-Gripaios-You 17
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CrivellinEtAl18"} Crivellin et al. 18
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Isidori19"} Isidori 19, slide 6
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/IsidoriExpectations19.jpg", :width => "610px"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            Outlook on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Belle+II+experiement"} Belle II experiement
            to confirm the flavour anomalies, if real (
            %a{:href => "#HHJLQV20"}> HHJLQV 20
            ):
          %blockquote
            %p
              With
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              …
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Belle+II"} Belle II
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+physics"} flavour physics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              we present a phenomenological study of the potential for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Belle+II"} Belle II
              to reveal possible new physics in the inclusive decay channel
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#HHJLQV20"}> p. 15
              \:) We see that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} anomalies
              in the exclusive sector can be confirmed at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significance"} 5σ
              level by inclusive measurements if the true values of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mn 9
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 10
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi NP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{9,10}^{\mu NP}
              are at the current best-fit point of the exclusive fits
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#HHJLQV20"}> p. 16
              \:) After including
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi s
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi μ
                        %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_s \to \mu^+ \mu_-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 9
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi NP
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 10
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi NP
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C_9^{\mu NP}, C_{10}^{\mu NP}]
              plane improves considerably. Exclusive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} anomalies
              could be confirmed at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significance"} 6σ
              level.
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#HHJLQV20"}> p. 20
              \:) Should the true value of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 9
                      %mi NP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_9^{NP}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 10
                      %mi NP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{10}^{NP}
              be at the current best-fit points of the global fits, an analysis of inclusive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar B_ \to X_s \ell^+ \ell^-
              at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Belle+II"} Belle II
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 50
                    %msup
                      %mi ab
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 50 ab^{-1}
              of data will exclude the SM point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 9
                      %mi NP
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 10
                      %mi NP
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_9^{NP} = C_{10}^{NP} = 0
              at the level of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∼
                    %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim 5
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significance"} σ
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar B_ \to X_s \ell^+ \ell^-
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Belle+II"} Belle II
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#GuadagnoliKoppenburg22"} Guadagnoli &amp; Koppenburg 2022
          %blockquote
            %p The main final message is that all the instruments necessary to fully establish the putative new effects are at hand, thanks to running experiments and their upgrades. Therefore this subject stands concrete chances to usher genuinely unexpected discoveries.
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#possible_models Possible models
          %p
            Candidate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} models
            of “New Physics” beyond the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            that could possibly explain the flavour anomalies (if indeed they are real) includes the following:
          %h3#Leptoquarks Leptoquarks and Grand unified theory
          %p
            One promising
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            that could potentially explain the apparently observed flavour anomalies are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leptoquarks"} leptoquarks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/grand+unified+theory"} grand unified theory
            (GUT)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pati-Salam+model"} Pati-Salam model
            (
            %a{:href => "#HeekTeresi18"}> Heek-Teresi 18
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HeekTeresi19"} Heek-Teresi 19
          %p
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BauerNeubert15"} Bauer-Neubert 15
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CCDM16"} CCDM 16
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Crivellin17"} Crivellin 17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Falkowski17"} Falkowski17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Mueller18"} Mueller 18
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MatsuzakiNishiwaki18"} Matsuzaki-Nishiwaki 18
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MonteuxRajaraman18"} Monteux-Rajaraman 18
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AMST18"} AMST 18
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BDFKFS18"} BDFKFS 18
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Crivellin18"} Crivellin 18
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MMR18"} MMR 18
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KumarLondon19"} Kumar-London 19, section 2.2.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MVT19"} MVT 19
            = succeed "," do
